{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAFzD2BGUnNZDLtXQ7RE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I finished the campaign and submitted index 12 (Sb fraction 0.723) as the best composition. It had the highest EQE I measured, at 0.00346%.\n\nI used all 5 EQE measurements and none of the 5 XRD measurements. I aimed the first measurements near CuSb₂O₆, a copper antimonate photoanode that sits at Sb 0.667. That choice came from my memory of the literature, not from anything the tools returned.\n\n| Index | Sb fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 8 | 0.580 | 0.00100 |\n| 10 | 0.653 | 0.00292 |\n| 11 | 0.689 | 0.00029 |\n| **12** | **0.723** | **0.00346** |\n| 15 | 0.805 | 0.00008 |\n\nEQE rises from 0.58 to 0.72 and has almost vanished by 0.80. A curve fit through three of the points put the peak near 0.70, so I spent the last measurement on index 11 (0.689). It came back about ten times lower than both of its neighbours. So the response along the line is either noisy or genuinely uneven, and the fitted peak can't be trusted.\n\nBecause of that dip, I can't say whether index 12 is the true best. The 0.723–0.80 range (indices 13 and 14) is untested and could beat it. XRD on index 11 might have explained the dip, but I didn't run any phase identification, so I have no structural explanation for any of these results."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":482,"cache_read_input_tokens":6594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":482},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e386a50d-708b-4b43-8829-35c1cc9d62e0","uuid":"647a80dd-61e1-42d3-85e3-42b4ad2c912d","timestamp":"2026-09-18T04:17:23.151Z","request_id":"req_011CfAFzCc89bSeHnHnGz